<h2>ClamAV is unreachable</h2>

<p>
  <strong><%= @site %></strong> cannot reach the ClamAV daemon at
  <strong><%= @target %></strong>.
</p>

<p>
  <strong>While this lasts, uploaded files are accepted and served without being
  scanned.</strong> File pushes are scanned in the background <em>after</em> the
  push is already live, so nothing blocks or fails visibly — the scan simply
  never happens.
</p>

<p>
  <strong>Unreachable since:</strong>
  <%= @down_since.in_time_zone("America/Chicago").strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M %Z") %>
  (<%= @downtime %>)
</p>

<h3>What to check</h3>
<p>
  The container can report <code>Up</code> while the daemon inside it is dead, so
  check the daemon rather than the container:
</p>
<pre>
docker exec pwpush-clamav ps -o pid,rss,args
docker exec pwpush-clamav sh -c 'netstat -ltn | grep 3310'
</pre>
<p>
  A <code>clamd</code> entry shown in brackets with <code>RSS 0</code> is a zombie
  — the daemon has died. Restarting the container usually restores it:
</p>
<pre>docker restart pwpush-clamav</pre>
<p>
  Afterwards, verify with a real detection test rather than a port check — a
  listening socket does not prove the signature database loaded.
</p>

<p>
  You will get another reminder if this is still unresolved later, and a single
  confirmation once it recovers.
</p>
